      "id": "uk-gdpr-article-5",
      "title": "UK GDPR Article 5",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/eur/2016/679/article/5",
      "last_verified": "2026-11-05",
      "stale_applicable": true,
      "opened": true,
      "note": "Opened on 5 November 2026. Article 5(1)(d) says personal data shall be accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date; every reasonable step must be taken to ensure that personal data that are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed, are erased or rectified without delay ('accuracy'). That paragraph had no footnote marker. Footnotes on the page were on Article 5(1)(b), Article 5(1)(e), and the inserted Article 5(3). This starter does not erase or rectify anything.",
      "age_days": 0,
      "stale": false
    },
